HIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMESUE, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORII, YUJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOYOTA JIDOSHA KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKADA MASAHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAMESUE KAZUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORII YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKADA, MASAHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAMESUE, KAZUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORII, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A battery unit (20) comprises a number of cells connected in series, and a voltage detector (13) is connected with each cell block (19) consisting of a plurality of cells. In the voltage detection circuit (13), the voltage across each cell block (19) is detected by a differential amplifier (2), converted to digital form, and applied to a controller through a photocoupler (7). The differential amplifier (2) and the cell block (19) are connected through optical relays (5, 6), which are closed by an ON/OFF control signal only when voltage is detected, so that no current leakage occurs. The differential amplifier (2) and an analog-to-digital converter (3) are powered by the cell block (19) through regulators (11, 12), respectively, to eliminate the effects of noise.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Unité batterie (20) qui comporte un certain nombre d'éléments connectés en série, un détecteur de tension (113) étant connecté à chaque bloc (19) d'éléments constitué d'une pluralité d'éléments. Dans le circuit (13) de détection de tension, la tension à chaque bloc (19) d'éléments est détectée par un amplificateur différentiel (2), convertie sous forme numérique et appliquée à un dispositif de commande par l'intermédiaire d'un photocoupleur (7). L'amplificateur différentiel (2) et le bloc (19) d'éléments sont connectés par l'intermédiaire de relais optiques (5, 6) qui sont fermés par un signal de commande marche/arrêt uniquement lorsque la tension est détectée, si bien qu'aucune fuite de courant ne se produit. L'amplificateur différentiel (2) et un convertisseur analogique-numérique (3) sont alimentés en puissance par le bloc (19) d'éléments à travers des régulateurs (11, 12) respectivement, pour éliminer les effets du bruit.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>